  "reading": "sigma_r is estimated from six and nine model judges, so its own interval spans roughly a factor of 4.0. The manuscript therefore reports the interval and the conclusion that holds across all of it: a source-level analysis is correctly calibrated only at sigma_r = 0, and at every value inside the anchored envelope it rejects a true null well above nominal, while both reviewer-level analyses hold the nominal level throughout. No point value of sigma_r is offered as a design constant, and the twelve-reviewer power figure is stated as an illustration at one point of that envelope rather than as a recommendation derived from a measured parameter.",
